{
  "_README": "EDIT THIS FILE BY HAND to shape the achievements feature - no code needed. The mockup page (achievements-mockup.html) renders straight from here, so any change you save shows up on refresh. Fields you'll usually touch: name, req (the short line on the badge), description (longer flavour text), availability, icon.emoji (placeholder) / icon.file (path Codex fills with a generated icon). 'id' is the stable key - keep it unique and DON'T rename it once an icon or save-data is tied to it. 'criteria' is the machine-readable unlock rule for when the feature is built; leave it unless you're changing what triggers the badge. 'hidden:true' marks a secret/easter-egg badge. 'availability.status:draft' means the achievement is designed but should not be shown on the live page until its required legends/tags exist. 'note' carries any feasibility caveat. To add a badge: copy an item, give it a new id. To remove one: delete the item.",
  "_criteria_help": {
    "count": "{type:count, scope:total|category|region|tag, value:<cat/region/tag>, n:<number>} - or {all:true} instead of n to mean 'every one'",
    "regions_all": "{type:regions_all, values:[...] } - visit at least one in each listed region tag",
    "category_all": "{type:category_all} - visit at least one legend in every category",
    "specific": "{type:specific, names:[...]} exact entry name(s), or {match:'kelpie'} to match any entry by name/tag substring",
    "behaviour": "{type:behaviour, kind:after_midnight|streak|visits, days/n:<number>} - client-side behaviour, not legend data"
  },
